/target
# `crates/*/target` and `anchor/target`: the sub-crates and the anchor app are deliberately plain
# path dependencies / a separate single-package build rather than workspace members (see the comment
# in Cargo.toml), so each builds into its own `target/` rather than sharing the root one. laze
# builds both apps into `/build` instead; these only appear when `cargo` is run directly, e.g. by
# `cargo fmt` or `cargo test`.
crates/*/target
tools/*/target
anchor/target
/build
.gdb_history
.direnv
